=== Parity notes ===
- Port of web/src/lib/globalShortcuts.tsx (GlobalShortcuts(): null) -- a REGISTRATION PROVIDER, not a visible view. Mounted once from the host root, it resolves the localized catalogue, registers it into the shared ShortcutRegistry for the composition lifetime, emits one PII-safe view.opened, and renders nothing (web "Returns nothing visible -- its only job is to populate the registry"). The grouped cheatsheet that READS the registry is a separate surface (KeyboardShortcutsModal, A-0006); rendering one here would duplicate it and invent UI the web spec lacks -- forbidden (no parity shortcuts / no silent drift).
- Catalogue = 21 definitions in the exact web order: 4 universals (Ctrl+K / "/" / "?" / Esc), 14 g+letter navigation entries (web Object.entries(GOTO_SHORTCUTS).map), 3 command-palette hints (web commandRegistry.filter(c => c.shortcut): themePicker T / shortcuts ? / dashboard.edit E). Every web id (global.palette.ctrlk, global.goto.{key}, global.palette.cmd.{commandId}), key-cap token, group, and scope='global' reproduced one-for-one; verified off-device in GlobalShortcutsProjectionTest.
- ShortcutRegistry is the P1/S8 StateFlow holder (web useShortcutRegistry external store): id-keyed, last-writer-wins, registration order preserved. A DisposableEffect registers on entering composition and unregisters the same ids on leaving it (web useShortcut effect + cleanup), keyed on the resolved definitions' structural value so a locale change re-registers but an incidental recomposition does not.
- No loading/error/stale/offline lifecycle: the surface has no async data source (only the i18n catalog + static GOTO/command tables), so modelling those states would fabricate behaviour the web spec lacks -- the same rationale the accepted QuickNav / QuickLinksSection ports document.
- i18n: group titles + descriptions resolve through the P1/S10 catalog at the Compose boundary; no English literal in native code. The goto description interpolates each destination's localized nav title (web interpolates the raw GOTO_SHORTCUTS label) -- Vehicles -> "Fleet", Battery -> "Battery Health" are documented, never-silent refinements. Key-cap tokens (Ctrl/K/"/"/"?"/Esc/g/letters/T/E) are reproduced verbatim: keyboard key identifiers, not translatable copy (the web does not translate them either).
- Accessibility: the provider emits no interactive element (it renders nothing), so there is no TalkBack node to label; GlobalShortcutsUiTest asserts the provider introduces no semantics node and that no registered description is drawn here. view.opened carries only the surface slug "globalShortcuts" (PII-safe).
- Gate path: settings.gradle.kts pins the app module to ':android' (the prompt's ':app:' is a template typo); the gate ran the real ':android' build/test/lint. The gate runs :android:testReleaseUnitTest (src/test) -- it does not compile src/androidTest; pre-existing androidTest mis-imports (assertExists/assertDoesNotExist) in OTHER surfaces are unrelated to this change and were left untouched.

